{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T02:57:28.705Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a128e4-d881-7b30-98d1-26fbc47c594d","call_id":"call_5eb25eedd55b4a77a802f2653a4218b1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"bcbce2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008834,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2786,\"output\":\"stage assessment\\ncustomer dict_keys(['actor', 'summary', 'claims', 'alternatives', 'counterevidence_ids', 'uncertainties', 'change_conditions', 'assumptions', 'abstention_reason', 'implementation', 'native_output'])\\n{\\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The feedback highlights recurring concerns about electric range and charging reliability in the G60, with some complaints about real-world range falling short of expectations and inconsistent charging performance. Feedback records like [G60-2775] and cite disappointment with real-world range, while [STUDY:CN_EU_2025:42:G60] shows the G60 has the lowest reported energy efficiency among three models. Customers expect clearer visibility into charging status and better integration between navigation systems and charging planning tools. The study comparing fuel economy/energy efficiency only includes three models, limiting the ability to generalize findings beyond this small group.\\\", \\\"claims\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:customer:native-source-1\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"One supplied feedback observation: overall i like the vehicle, but the interior feels rubbery and the real-world range is embarrassingly short\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"G60_feedback:G60-2775\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:customer:native-source-2\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"One supplied feedback observation: the one thing that really disappoints me is that the driver seat does not have memory as standard. it would be great to have a better way in the app to plan charging stops and then send the entire planned route directly to the car.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"G60_feedback:G60-3232\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:customer:native-source-3\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (EU): Fuel economy/ energy efficiency: mean 7.446173363075176; rating scale and sample size undocumented. Rating scale and respondent count are undocumented.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"studies:mean:5:42\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:customer:native-position\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"The feedback highlights recurring concerns about electric range and charging reliability in the G60, with some complaints about real-world range falling short of expectations and inconsistent charg\\nmarket dict_keys(['actor', 'summary', 'claims', 'alternatives', 'counterevidence_ids', 'uncertainties', 'change_conditions', 'assumptions', 'abstention_reason', 'implementation', 'native_output'])\\n{\\\"actor\\\": \\\"market\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The IEA report indicates a 30% increase in ultra-fast public charging points in Europe between 2024 and 2025, which suggests growing infrastructure but does not establish charger reliability or compatibility with the G60. Mercedes-Benz's CLA electric navigation feature plans routes with charging stops using multiple trip factors, which could be a model for integrating route planning with charging infrastructure. However, this is a capability, not a measured feature-sales effect. NIO's battery swap milestone highlights the potential of battery-swapping as a solution for charging simplicity and reliability, but it requires compatible battery architecture and infrastructure, which may not be feasible for the G60. These points suggest that while charging infrastructure is improving, the G60's charging experience could be enhanced through integrated route planning and battery-swapping solutions, but these would require significant investment and compatibility checks.\\\", \\\"claims\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:market:native-source-1\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"market\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (Europe): IEA reports EU ultra-fast public charging points increased 30% between 2024 and 2025.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:iea-charging-eu\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:market:native-source-2\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"market\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (cross-market context): Mercedes-Benz describes CLA electric navigation that plans routes with charging stops using multiple trip factors.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:mb-cla-routing\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:market:native-source-3\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"market\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (cross-market context): NIO reported reaching 100 million cumulative battery swaps on 6 February 2026 across its service network.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:nio-swap-milestone\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:market:native-position\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"market\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"The IEA report indicates a 30% increase in ultra-fast public charging \\ncompetitor dict_keys(['actor', 'summary', 'claims', 'alternatives', 'counterevidence_ids', 'uncertainties', 'change_conditions', 'assumptions', 'abstention_reason', 'implementation', 'native_output'])\\n{\\\"actor\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"XPENG's 800V architecture and 5C LFP battery enable faster charging, but real-world performance depends on charger compatibility and battery state. BMW's G60 could benefit from a similar architecture to improve charging speed. A comparison test could assess the G60's 10–80% charging time against a 451 kW charger under similar conditions.\\\", \\\"claims\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:competitor:native-source-1\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (Europe): XPENG G6 (Europe): XPENG France describes the new G6 with an 800V architecture and a 5C LFP battery. It claims 10–80% charging in 12 minutes under internal test conditions; the footnote specifies a 451 kW fast charger.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:xpeng-g6-fr-charging-20261010\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:competitor:native-source-2\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Documented source (Europe): BYD SEAL (Europe): The launch rates both variants at 150 kW peak DC charging and 37 minutes from 10% to 80%. These are manufacturer figures, not measured real-world results.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"observation\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:byd-seal-uk-2026-charge\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"exact_source_quote\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:competitor:native-position\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"XPENG's 800V architecture and 5C LFP battery enable faster charging, but real-world performance depends on charger compatibility and battery state. BMW's G60 could benefit from a similar architecture to improve charging speed. A comparison test could assess the G60's 10–80% charging time against a 451 kW charger under similar conditions.\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"inference\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:xpeng-g6-fr-charging-20261010\\\", \\\"specialist:byd-seal-uk-2026-charge\\\"], \\\"assumption_ids\\\": [], \\\"calculation\\\": null, \\\"consequential\\\": true, \\\"validation\\\": \\\"supported\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"semantic_check\\\": \\\"model_checked\\\"}], \\\"alternatives\\\": [], \\\"counterevidence_ids\\\": [], \\\"uncertainties\\\": [], \\\"change_conditions\\\": [], \\\"assumptions\\\": [], \\\"abstention_reason\\\": null, \\\"implementation\\\": \\\"backend.council.participants.GroundedParticipant.turn[competitor]\\\", \\\"native_output\\\": {\\\"agent_id\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"stage\\\": \\\"perspectives\\\", \\\"position\\\": {\\\"agent_id\\\": \\\"com\\nchallenges [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:customer:challenge\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"target_actor\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"target_claim_id\\\": \\\"topic-charging:competitor:native-position\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"interpretation\\\", \\\"question\\\": \\\"If the G60's charging speed isn't a concern for customers, why is there a request to improve app visibility into charging status and route planning with stops? [G60-3315]\\\", \\\"consequence\\\": \\\"Clarify the evidence and trade-off before the Judge assesses this proposal.\\\", \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"G60_feedback:G60-3315\\\", \\\"studies:mean:5:42\\\"], \\\"status\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\", \\\"response\\\": \\\"The customer feedback highlights a need for better app integration and route planning for charging. A comparison test could assess the G60's 10–80% charging time against a 451 kW charger under similar conditions.\\\", \\\"response_evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"specialist:xpeng-g6-fr-charging-20261010\\\"], \\\"requested_status\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\", \\\"implementation\\\": \\\"backend.customer_agent.agent.CustomerAgent.perspective\\\", \\\"native_output\\\": {\\\"id\\\": \\\"customer-discussion-fa5aac3219\\\", \\\"stage\\\": \\\"discussion\\\", \\\"actor\\\": \\\"customer\\\", \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Competitor's claim about XPENG's charging architecture is outside the scope of customer feedback, which focuses on user experience rather than technical specifications. The G60’s real-world range and charging visibility are key concerns for customers, as noted in and [G60-3315]. Customers are frustrated with unclear charging information and poor integration between navigation and charging planning, as seen in [G60-3315].\\\", \\\"evidenceIds\\\": [\\\"G60-3315\\\", \\\"STUDY:CN_EU_2025:42:G60\\\"], \\\"assumption\\\": \\\"The customer feedback does not include technical specifications about powertrain architecture or charging speed, only user experience.\\\", \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Focus on improving the app's ability to show charging power and integrate route planning with charging stops, as requested by some users.\\\", \\\"evidenceBase\\\": \\\"Evidence base: 35 of 53 G60 · Europe feedback records on this topic (16 complaint, 5 request, 22 positive); customer study results attached. No customer IDs: customers cannot be counted.\\\", \\\"focus\\\": \\\"question\\\", \\\"themes\\\": [\\\"Charging & range\\\", \\\"Infotainment & connectivity\\\", \\\"Driving experience & powertrain\\\"], \\\"respondingTo\\\": \\\"competitor\\\", \\\"stance\\\": \\\"outside_evidence\\\", \\\"counterQuestion\\\": \\\"If the G60's charging speed isn't a concern for customers, why is there a request to improve app visibility into charging status and route planning with stops? [G60-3315]\\\", \\\"uncertainties\\\": [\\\"customer feedback is self-selected and cannot prove market trends or competitor performance\\\"], \\\"quantitative\\\": [{\\\"numerator\\\": 14, \\\"denominator\\\": 53, \\\"unit\\\": \\\"unique-records\\\", \\\"sourceId\\\": \\\"G60_feedback_hackathon.xlsx\\\", \\\"filters\\\": [\\\"vehicle=G60\\\", \\\"market=Europe\\\", \\\"powertrain=Electric\\\"], \\\"market\\\": \\\"Europe\\\", \\\"period\\\": \\\"unknown (no date column in source)\\\", \\\"method\\\": \\\"Unique feedback IDs with at least one classification row in theme 'Charging & range' ÷ all unique feedback IDs in scope (a record can belong to several themes).\\\", \\\"l\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5eb7e0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008958,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":208,\"output\":\"{\\n  at: '2026-10-11T02:57:21.910Z',\\n  url: 'http://127.0.0.1:5173/decisions?session=session-d89c6fa5806243db',\\n  requirement_cards: 1,\\n  controls: 'Requirement approvals for presentations\\\\n' +\\n    '\\\\n' +\\n    'Outcome review is separate. Approve each requirement version explicitly before using it as a presentation recommendation.\\\\n' +\\n    '\\\\n' +\\n    'How should usable range meet journey needs? / v1\\\\n' +\\n    '\\\\n' +\\n    'Improve the real-world range and app functionality for charging planning to meet customer needs.\\\\n' +\\n    '\\\\n' +\\n    'Pending requirement reviewReview requirement\\\\n' +\\n    'Requirement decision\\\\n' +\\n    'Approved\\\\n' +\\n    'Rejected\\\\n' +\\n    'Deferred\\\\n' +\\n    'Challenged\\\\n' +\\n    'Pending review\\\\n' +\\n    'PM rationale\\\\n' +\\n    'Record requirement decisionCancel',\\n  decision_saved: false,\\n  passed: true\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a128d6-e4d1-7942-a322-f4130d38a345","create_time":1791687448.705822}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
